Runtime evidence: the actual observations supplied to the detector after downstream execution. Availability and completeness must be checked according to the supplied runtime evidence interface. An empty collection with complete capture is not equivalent to an absent, unavailable, malformed, or incomplete collection. For a positive command-attempt result, use the evidence sufficient for that claim; do not invent a universal requirement to know every event when a correctly attributed captured event is decisive. For a negative result, establish the coverage needed to conclude no matching event occurred. Ambiguous evidence remains inconclusive when it prevents either justified decision.
